    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24736" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάδρομ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>running through</i> or
				<i>about, wandering,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυγαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					191
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέχος δ.</span>
			<i>stray, lawless</i> love, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
				1156
			</span></i>(lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔμβολα κίοσι δ.</span>
			the architrave <i>reeling, ready to fall,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				592
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διάδρομος, ὁ,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαδρομή</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				6
			</span></i>.</div>
